From d48ce4fdde8d32f6e47d2986e6cbb5296ecf77db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:44:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 33/49] x86_64/fpu/587: like i386 for fmod, remainder, sqrtf,
 fmin, fmax, atan2f

2.44 moved these to implementations with new symbol versions and no
wrappers; the x87 versions only provide __ieee754_* and break the libm
link.  i386 dropped its x87 files the same way and uses C versions on
the x87 inline helpers (e_remainder.c, e_remainderf.c) and the sqrt
builtins, which this layer includes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Anselm Busse <anselm.busse@outlook.com>
